From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvdisplay: adapt to pci_resize_resource() exclude_bars argument

Upstream commit 337b1b566db08 ("PCI: Fix restoring BARs on BAR resize
rollback path"), mainline v6.19 and backported to stable v6.18.40,
added a fourth argument to pci_resize_resource(): exclude_bars, a mask
of BARs that must NOT be released while the kernel now releases the
device resources sharing the bridge window by itself (previously the
caller had to release them, which nv-pci.c already does for BAR1/BAR3).

The reference Yocto build uses 6.18.22 (3-argument API) so it still
compiles there; Armbian ships 6.18.43 and the nvdisplay build dies with:

  nvidia/nv-pci.c:219:9: error: too few arguments to function
  'pci_resize_resource'; expected 4, have 3

Detect the new signature with a conftest arity probe instead of a
LINUX_VERSION_CODE check: the change lives in a stable branch, so any
distro kernel may or may not carry the backport regardless of version
number, and the tree already keys every other kernel-API difference off
conftest. Pass exclude_bars = 0 (nothing to protect), which preserves
the pre-change behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending [applicable to OE4T/nv-kernel-display-driver wip-r36.5-take-2]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>

diff --git a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
index 26a737e..5e5d73a 100644
--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/conftest.sh
@@ -6192,6 +6192,25 @@ compile_test() {
             compile_check_conftest "$CODE" "NV_PCI_REBAR_GET_POSSIBLE_SIZES_PRESENT" "" "functions"
         ;;
 
+        pci_resize_resource_has_exclude_bars_arg)
+            #
+            # Determine if pci_resize_resource() has the exclude_bars
+            # argument.
+            #
+            # Added by commit 337b1b566db08 ("PCI: Fix restoring BARs on
+            # BAR resize rollback path") in v6.19, backported to stable
+            # v6.18.40.
+            #
+            CODE="
+            #include <linux/pci.h>
+            int pci_resize_resource(struct pci_dev *dev, int i, int size,
+                                    int exclude_bars) {
+                return 0;
+            }"
+
+            compile_check_conftest "$CODE" "NV_PCI_RESIZE_RESOURCE_HAS_EXCLUDE_BARS_ARG" "" "types"
+        ;;
+
         wait_for_random_bytes)
             #
             # Determine if the wait_for_random_bytes() function is present.
diff --git a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
index ad2bfee..a400e9d 100644
--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
@@ -216,7 +216,19 @@ static int nv_resize_pcie_bars(struct pci_dev *pci_dev) {
 
 resize:
     /* Attempt to resize BAR1 to the largest supported size */
+#if defined(NV_PCI_RESIZE_RESOURCE_HAS_EXCLUDE_BARS_ARG)
+    /*
+     * Since commit 337b1b566db08 ("PCI: Fix restoring BARs on BAR resize
+     * rollback path", v6.19, stable v6.18.40) pci_resize_resource()
+     * releases the device resources sharing the bridge window by itself;
+     * exclude_bars is a mask of BARs that must NOT be released. We
+     * already released BAR1/BAR3 above and have nothing to protect, so
+     * pass 0 to keep the pre-change behavior.
+     */
+    r = pci_resize_resource(pci_dev, NV_GPU_BAR1, requested_size, 0);
+#else
     r = pci_resize_resource(pci_dev, NV_GPU_BAR1, requested_size);
+#endif
 
     if (r) {
         if (r == -ENOSPC)
diff --git a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nvidia.Kbuild b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nvidia.Kbuild
index 5d33def..a867870 100644
--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nvidia.Kbuild
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nvidia.Kbuild
@@ -249,6 +249,7 @@ NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += remove_memory_has_nid_arg
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += add_memory_driver_managed_has_mhp_flags_arg
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += num_registered_fb
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += pci_driver_has_driver_managed_dma
+NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += pci_resize_resource_has_exclude_bars_arg
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += vm_area_struct_has_const_vm_flags
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += memory_failure_has_trapno_arg
 NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += of_property_for_each_u32_has_internal_args
